  id: SQL_TYPE_01_SELECT
  language: 3
  topic: SELECT
  difficulty: 0
  questionType: 2
  questionText: Type the column name so the query shows only the witness of every
    sighting.
  code: 'Table: sightings

    +----+----------+-------+---------+

    | id | location
    | time  | witness |

    +----+----------+-------+---------+

    |  1 | Park    
    | 15:10 | Mia     |

    |  2 | Library  | 15:40 | Leo     |

    |  3 | Bus
    Stop | 16:05 | Ana     |

    |  4 | Arcade   | 15:25 | Leo     |

    +----+----------+-------+---------+


    SELECT
    ____ FROM sightings;'
  answerFormat: 1
  choices: []
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 0
  acceptedAnswers:
  - witness
  caseSensitive: 0
  referenceFill: 
  runTests: []
  explanation: SELECT lists the columns you want to see. SELECT witness FROM sightings
    shows only the witness column for every row.
  hint: SELECT is followed by the name of the column to show. Which column holds
    the names of the people?
  wrongChoiceFeedback: []
  wrongAnswerFeedback: Type just the column name that holds the witness names. Check
    the spelling against the table header.
